Asha leaves my flat.
Her dog Moti is very sad.
He paces here and there in the flat.
He misses Asha, and whines softly.
I must take care of him.
I look at him.
I sit on my rug on the floor.
I gently pat the rug with my hand.
I call him near me.
"Moti, come here," I say with affection.
"Sit here on the rug."
He comes near me, but he still whines.
I must calm that dog.
I take his favourite chew toy.
I hand that toy to him.
"Look at this toy," I say.
"Take it."
He takes that toy with his mouth.
He sits on the rug and chews that toy.
Now Moti is calm.
